\textbf{Result.} Dual-stream experts reduce the average DLinear gap from $+57\%$ to $+5\%$ (an $11\times$ reduction) and \emph{beat} DLinear on Weather ($0.198$ vs $0.208$, $p{=}0.03$, paired $t$-test). The learned blend parameters $\alpha_k \approx 0.49$ across all five experts confirm that the backbone provides complementary information on Weather and the other nonlinear-dynamics datasets when experts can also access the raw signal; on the linear-dominated datasets (ETTh2, ETTm2, Electricity) a TSFM-free raw-MLP MoE attains comparable or better MSE on its own (Appendix~\ref{app:raw_mlp_moe}), so the relative contribution of each branch is dataset-dependent.

